  "notes": "808 Mafia-affiliated dark trap with a cinematic top, and the identifying pair is chromatic-neighbour lead motion over a static tonic. `melody.halfStepDissonance` 0.3 with `intervals.step` 0.72 is the chromatic neighbour written as parameters — the melody moves by semitone around a centre rather than through a progression — and `register` [66,98] is the wide register spread the research names, the widest melodic span in this batch. The 808 is the other half: overdriven deliberately, so `distortion` is `heavy` with `distortionWet` [0.35,0.7] and `bassline.glideProb` 0.7 for the hard glides. Mid-track beat switches are `switchUpProb` 0.35, the highest here. ⚠ `low` confidence, and the research says why: it rates this medium-low, first-party interviews are thin, and it marks the tempo bounds [LOW-CONF] — `session.bpm` is therefore the least trustworthy field in this file. The drum numbers (`kick.densityPerBar`, `syncopation`) are inferred from \"hard syncopated 16th kicks\" alone. ⚠ `chords.impliedByRiff` is set because the harmony really is a static tonic under a moving lead. The i–VI–VII family is the research's \"occasional\" one and is weighted accordingly; the i–bII family at weight 1 is INFERRED from the chromatic-neighbour description and is the first thing to delete.",
